From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:01:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep hosted services and telemetry inactive

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Keep hosted services, telemetry, promotional content,
sponsored discovery, and automatic onboarding present but never active
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1001-personal-provider-openrouter-eu-and-auth-provider-selection.patch, 1003-personal-feature-worker-blueprints-and-session-lifecycle-fixes.patch
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 1007-personal-feature-disable-hosted-services-telemetry-and-promotions.patch

Patch intent:
The personal build keeps upstream's hosted service code but never activates,
shows, or reaches it. No telemetry is collected, shown, or sent. The jcode
hosted provider is denied unless listed in allowed_providers and is never the
default or auto-selected. jcode account, subscription, billing, upgrade, and
marketing surfaces are hidden and rejected. compile_remote and the sponsored
integration directory tool are not registered, and sponsored discovery is
forced off. Automatic onboarding never starts, manual rehearsal stays, and
login import needs an explicit Continue. Jev features keep working with the
user's own providers but never route to the jcode gateway. Jade cloud sessions
and the Jade relay are hidden, rejected, and never started. The /remote cloud
sales link is hidden while the local /remote gateway, /cloud, and /local stay.

Why it exists:
The personal build runs without hosted accounts, tiers, billing, telemetry,
ads, sponsors, or nudges. Gating at chokepoints instead of deleting code keeps
the patch small and the rebase cost low.

The swarm completion-report instruction test in server/swarm.rs pins the
shared text jcode-swarm-core appends to worker prompts. Its expected string
now matches that shared wording verbatim (otherwise include a concise
summary, validation/tests performed, and blockers or follow-ups) instead of
a mis-cased paraphrase, and the idempotence assertions are unchanged. The
appended instruction text itself does not change.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-telemetry-core/src/lib.rs is_enabled (false outside tests),
telemetry and transcript endpoints (None), send and post payload guards,
oauth_account.rs enqueue, send, check, upload, and notice paths,
concurrency.rs begin_concurrency_session, jcode-app-core agent.rs
upload_transcript_telemetry, TUI oauth_telemetry.rs and tui_state.rs notices.
Provider family policy constructor (jcode-provider-core and
jcode-base/src/provider_catalog.rs) denies the jcode family unless listed,
provider/jcode.rs, provider auto-default selection, login catalogs, usage.rs
upgrade hints, TUI auth_account_commands.rs, commands.rs, input_help.rs,
state_ui_input_helpers.rs, subscribe_nudge.rs, src/cli/args.rs, dispatch.rs,
provider_init.rs. Tool registry construction in jcode-app-core/src/tool
(compile_remote, integration_tools), sponsors config, onboarding startup and
import flow in jcode-tui. jcode-base/src/jev.rs, gateway/control.rs,
jcode-app-core channel.rs, server.rs and server/jade_relay.rs,
runtime_special_commands.rs, TUI commands_remote.rs,
src/cli/args/cloud_sessions.rs.
Inactive modules carry allow(dead_code) with a comment naming this patch.

Update guidance:
When upstream adds a hosted, account, telemetry, sponsor, or marketing path,
gate it at its chokepoint rather than deleting code. Every telemetry producer
must return before creating identities, files, queues, or requests when
is_enabled is false. Never let an explicit jcode selection fall back silently
to another credential. Keep /cloud, /local, the local /remote gateway, Jev
with user providers, manual onboarding rehearsal, and provider login and
import working.

